---
description: Non-negotiable invariants for the D2D platform
alwaysApply: true
---

- Coverage is DERIVED from knock_events. Never create a coverage table.
- No scoring, ranking or quality signals in any `/field` route. Admin only. Eligibility facts (NCCZ, do_not_call, no_opportunity) may persist in `/field`. Quality signals may not. Current-assignment outcome colour is permitted; previous-visit outcome colour is not.
- All field writes go through `lib/sync/queue.ts`. Never a second sync path.
- Every client-originated write carries a `client_event_id`. Re-sync is idempotent.
- PostGIS columns are `geometry(Point,4326)` / `geometry(Polygon,4326)`. Cast `::geography` for distance only.
- RLS enabled with default-deny on every table.
- Raw GPS coordinates never leave the device. Only a distance-along-route scalar.
- Teams bunny-hop (1 to 3 people): same side, same route, leapfrogging door to door. No side split, no per-canvasser door allocation. Do not redesign this.
- Service role key is server-only, never in a `NEXT_PUBLIC_` var.
- British English in user-facing strings.
- One stage per session. Never start the next stage.
- Address text is a display label only. UPRN is the only door identity. A house number may be typed against an ALREADY-SELECTED UPRN and stored in `address_observations`. Address search, autocomplete, street/postcode entry and address-as-identifier remain banned.
- `property_addresses` is a separate table. Never denormalise `house_number`, `street_name`, `building_name` or `sub_building` into `properties`, `knock_events`, `leads` or `uprn_snapshot`.
- Later address ingest passes never overwrite a higher-confidence earlier pass.
- Stages 0–7 and 1c built; 8a in progress. Read `supabase/migrations/` for the next free number. Never edit an applied migration. Never assume a number.
- `knock_events.outcome` has nine values including `no_opportunity`.
- `address_observations` is the highest address-confidence tier; resolve labels through `v_door_label`, never by reading `property_addresses` directly in a field component.
- No `navigator.geolocation` before Stage 16.
- Every view over an RLS table needs `(security_invoker = true)`.
